# Bundled broker ACL (copied by mosquitto-init next to the password file).
# zigbee2mqtt: the bridge; homeassistant: Home Assistant's MQTT integration.
# Both get the base topic and Home Assistant's discovery prefix, nothing else.
# Mosquitto 2.1 (plugins/acl-file): "deny" entries are checked before every
# grant of the user and refuse both read and write, so homeassistant can
# never install code into Zigbee2MQTT (external extensions / converters),
# change its options (e.g. the MQTT server), or request / read a backup
# (the coordinator backup holds the network key).
user zigbee2mqtt
topic readwrite zigbee2mqtt/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

user homeassistant
topic deny zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/extension/#
topic deny zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/converter/#
topic deny zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/backup
topic deny zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/options
topic deny zigbee2mqtt/bridge/response/backup
topic readwrite zigbee2mqtt/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#
